{"name":"Noodle Arms","hex":"#f5ddc4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"noodle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A string or flat strip of pasta or other dough, usually cooked (at least initially) by boiling, and served in soup or in a dry form mixed with a sauce and other ingredients.","An object which is long and thin like a noodle (sense 1)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person with poor judgment; a fool.","The brain; the head."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noodle"},{"term":"arms","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Weaponry, weapons.","A visual design composed according to heraldic rules, normally displayed upon an escutcheon and sometimes accompanied by other elements of an achievement"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of arm"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arms"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arms (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Arms is a 2017 fighting game developed and published by Nintendo for the Nintendo Switch. The game differentiates itself from standard fighting games with its unconventional fighting system where every playable character fights with long range attacks and up to four players can choose a fighter and battle using a variety of extendable, weaponized arms to knock out opponents in a three-dimensional arena. Arms received generally favorable reviews from critics and sold over two million copies by July 2018."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cc/Arms_%28video_game%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arms_(video_game)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cc/Arms_%28video_game%29.jpg/250px-Arms_%28video_game%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cc/Arms_%28video_game%29.jpg?utm_source=e